1
00:01:46,104 --> 00:01:47,562
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ

2
00:01:48,804 --> 00:01:50,112
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ

3
00:01:51,140 --> 00:01:57,208
اَلْحَمْدُ لله رَبِّ الّعَالَمِيْن، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

4
00:01:57,910 --> 00:01:59,359
السلام عليكم ورحمةالله

5
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:06,758
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to bless this gathering and we ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to make it beneficial for all of us,

6
00:02:08,477 --> 00:02:13,205
نَسْعَلُ الله عزوجل اَنْ يَرْزُقْنَا الْجَنَّةْ وَنَعُوْذُبِهِ مِنَّ النَّار

7
00:02:13,685 --> 00:02:17,963
رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ

8
00:02:19,856 --> 00:02:22,876
صلى الله على سيدنا محمد وعلى آله وصحبه وسلم

9
00:02:25,683 --> 00:02:34,477
For the past few weeks, preparing for this series of talks on Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

10
00:02:36,497 --> 00:02:39,867
I got to do some reading about Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

11
00:02:40,792 --> 00:02:51,930
Now, we all know that Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) is the greatest, after the Anbiyaa(انبياء) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

12
00:02:53,759 --> 00:03:01,307
But somehow we always have this, special love of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه,

13
00:03:03,549 --> 00:03:04,897
everybody is impressed with him.

14
00:03:05,932 --> 00:03:11,442
With the personality of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), the power and strength of Al-Farooque(الفاروق).

15
00:03:13,855 --> 00:03:22,115
So, sometimes we don't do a lot of studying on the Siddique رضي الله عنه.

16
00:03:24,505 --> 00:03:32,101
So, in the past weeks I had a chance to be, exposed in detail to his personality.

17
00:03:33,022 --> 00:03:39,340
And Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), his personality is amazing, surprising.

18
00:03:41,733 --> 00:03:49,527
Because whenever you pull out a list of a good deed, you would find the name of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) on the top.

19
00:03:53,222 --> 00:03:56,972
Whichever list, you pull out, you're going to find his name on there and it's the first name.

20
00:03:58,536 --> 00:03:59,699
He was the first Muslim,

21
00:04:00,425 --> 00:04:01,639
he was the first Khalifah(خليفه),

22
00:04:02,504 --> 00:04:05,883
he was the first and only person to be with Rasool Allah ﷺ on Al-Hijrah(ألهجرة).

23
00:04:07,445 --> 00:04:08,656
He was the first on Eeman(ايمان),

24
00:04:08,696 --> 00:04:12,429
Rasool Allah ﷺ says, that the Eeman(ايمان) of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is greater than all of the Ummah(أمة).

25
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:19,447
Even on issues that we would regard as normal deeds.

26
00:04:20,665 --> 00:04:23,911
Rasool Allah ﷺ was once sitting in the Masjid(مسجد) and he asked the Sahabah(صحابه),

27
00:04:24,721 --> 00:04:25,848
who's fasting this day?

28
00:04:26,951 --> 00:04:28,373
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) said: I am!

29
00:04:29,434 --> 00:04:31,175
Who has visited an ill person.?

30
00:04:31,831 --> 00:04:33,307
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) said: I did!

31
00:04:34,296 --> 00:04:35,865
Who has followed a Janazah(جنازه).?

32
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:38,058
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) said: I did!

33
00:04:38,774 --> 00:04:40,992
Who on this day, has given out Sadaqah(صدقه).?

34
00:04:41,431 --> 00:04:42,926
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) said: I did!

35
00:04:43,187 --> 00:04:47,835
And everybody else in the Masjid(مسجد) is looking around and the only hand that is going up is the hand of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

36
00:04:49,394 --> 00:04:52,136
In fact, in another narration of this.

37
00:04:52,620 --> 00:04:54,654
It says that this happened after Salat-Ul-Fajr(صلاة الفجر)

38
00:04:54,950 --> 00:04:57,114
because Rasool Allah ﷺ used to meet with the Sahabah(صحابه),

39
00:04:57,442 --> 00:05:01,289
after Salat-Ul-Fajr(صلاة الفجر) and talk with them in the Masjid(مسجد), after Salah(صلاة), they would talk.

40
00:05:01,627 --> 00:05:03,410
For example, they would talk about dreams,

41
00:05:03,712 --> 00:05:05,696
they would talk about different issues.

42
00:05:05,742 --> 00:05:10,296
Rasool Allah ﷺ would spend time with the Sahabah(صحابه) after Salat-Ul-Fajr(صلاة الفجر), conversing with them.

43
00:05:11,697 --> 00:05:15,422
So it says, Rasool Allah ﷺ asked, Who has followed the Janazah(جنازه).?

44
00:05:15,462 --> 00:05:17,651
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: We just started our day!

45
00:05:18,665 --> 00:05:20,649
And then he said: Who has given Sadaqah(صدقه).?

46
00:05:20,903 --> 00:05:23,077
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), We just started our day!

47
00:05:23,101 --> 00:05:25,959
But Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said:

48
00:05:26,495 --> 00:05:30,213
When I was coming to the Masjid(مسجد), I saw a poor man outside, so I gave him Sadaqah(صدقه).

49
00:05:30,993 --> 00:05:32,803
So who has visited an ill person.?

50
00:05:33,343 --> 00:05:34,835
 Umar(عمر) said: We just started our day.

51
00:05:34,874 --> 00:05:37,437
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق) said: I heard that Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) was ill,

52
00:05:37,461 --> 00:05:39,839
so before I came to the Masjid(مسجد), I went to visit him.

53
00:05:40,336 --> 00:05:45,072
So whenever Rasool Allah ﷺ would ask a question, it's Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) who would say: I did it.

54
00:05:45,426 --> 00:05:51,354
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: If these deeds combined together in one person, that person is going to Jannah(جنة).

55
00:05:53,270 --> 00:05:57,651
So again, whatever list you look at, you would find Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) on the top of it.

56
00:05:58,890 --> 00:06:01,028
Ali Bin Abi Talib رضي الله عنه says,

57
00:06:01,706 --> 00:06:02,614
هُوَ سَبَّاقْ

58
00:06:03,158 --> 00:06:04,006
He was the first.

59
00:06:05,415 --> 00:06:09,523
And whenever we would compete with him on any deed, he would come ahead of us.

60
00:06:10,305 --> 00:06:13,881
And that's a statement made by Ali Bin Abi Talib رضي الله عنه.

61
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:14,917
And we know the story

62
00:06:15,483 --> 00:06:18,936
when Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wanted to compete with Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

63
00:06:18,976 --> 00:06:20,127
and keep in mind

64
00:06:20,708 --> 00:06:23,406
that competition in good, is good.

65
00:06:24,014 --> 00:06:27,012
Competition in good deeds, is a good deed.

66
00:06:27,738 --> 00:06:31,846
See in Islam, we're not supposed to compete on worldly affairs,

67
00:06:31,886 --> 00:06:33,523
we're not supposed to compete on Duniyah(دنيا)

68
00:06:33,815 --> 00:06:35,786
when it comes to Duniyah(دنيا), Rasool Allah ﷺ says,

69
00:06:36,027 --> 00:06:37,540
فَاتَّقُو الله وَاَجْمِلُوْا فِي الطَّلَبْ

70
00:06:38,425 --> 00:06:41,853
Have Taqwa(تقوى) of Allah, and take it easy when it comes to Duniyah(دنيا).

71
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:45,967
نَفْسًا رُوح الْقُدُس فِي رَوعِيْ اَنَّه’ لَنْ تَمُوتَ نَفْسٌ

72
00:06:46,308 --> 00:06:50,753
حَتَّى تَقْضِي اَجَلَهَا وَتَسْتَوْفِيَ رِزْقَهَا  فَاتَّقُوا اللهَ ، وَأَجْمِلُوا فِي الطَّلَبِ

73
00:06:51,471 --> 00:06:56,059
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: The Holy Spirit, Jibreel عليه السّلام has inspired to me

74
00:06:56,488 --> 00:07:02,147
that no one would die until they reach the end of their life, their prescribed life,

75
00:07:02,406 --> 00:07:04,661
and until they get all of their provisions.

76
00:07:05,016 --> 00:07:06,254
So, take it easy in Duniyah(دنيا).

77
00:07:06,433 --> 00:07:07,976
فَاتَّقُوا اللهَ ، وَأَجْمِلُوا فِي الطَّلَبِ

78
00:07:08,766 --> 00:07:13,391
So look at Duniyah(دنيا), Rasool Allah ﷺ says, Calm down, take it easy.

79
00:07:14,434 --> 00:07:16,992
But look at the terminology that was used with Aakhirah(آخرة).

80
00:07:17,703 --> 00:07:19,134
In Qur'an Allah سبحانه تعالى says:

81
00:07:19,158 --> 00:07:20,320
سَابِقُوا إِلَىٰ وَجَنَّةٍ

82
00:07:20,792 --> 00:07:21,971
وَسَارِعُوا إِلَىٰ  وَجَنَّةٍ

83
00:07:22,451 --> 00:07:25,519
كَانُوا يُسَارِعُونَ فِي الْخَيْرَاتِ وَيَدْعُونَنَا رَغَبًا وَرَهَبًا

84
00:07:25,968 --> 00:07:28,143
The words used, when it comes to Aakhirah(آخرة) is compete

85
00:07:28,283 --> 00:07:30,237
وَفِي ذَٰلِكَ فَلْيَتَنَافَسِ الْمُتَنَافِسُونَ

86
00:07:30,662 --> 00:07:33,868
Sabiqoo(سابقو) race! Sarioo(سارعو) - hasten!

87
00:07:34,491 --> 00:07:39,594
So, when it comes to Aakhirah(آخرة), you need to compete and think about it as a race

88
00:07:39,741 --> 00:07:43,309
you're in competition because there's specific places in Jannah(جنة)

89
00:07:43,710 --> 00:07:49,942
and out of every 1000 human beings only one will make it to Jannah(جنة)

90
00:07:50,021 --> 00:07:53,778
 Nine hundred ninety nine(999) are going to Hellfire according to the Hadith(حديث) in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم).

91
00:07:53,988 --> 00:07:56,442
Allahعَزّوجَلّ will bring Adam عليه السّلام and tell him,

92
00:07:56,466 --> 00:07:57,350
أخْرِجْ بَعثَ النَّار

93
00:07:57,731 --> 00:08:01,276
Send out the portion of your children that are going to hellfire.

94
00:08:01,562 --> 00:08:02,990
So, Adam عليه السّلام will say,

95
00:08:03,014 --> 00:08:03,823
وَمَا بَعْثَ النَّار

96
00:08:04,176 --> 00:08:07,044
What portion of my children are going to hellfire.?

97
00:08:07,350 --> 00:08:10,818
Allahعَزّوجَلّ will tell Adam(آدم) out of every thousand, 999!

98
00:08:11,465 --> 00:08:14,450
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was ahead.

99
00:08:15,982 --> 00:08:20,414
And that's something that you noticed throughout his life, he would always come out the first.

100
00:08:21,442 --> 00:08:27,430
And the amazing thing is that it didn't seem as if Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was doing it to compete with anyone.

101
00:08:28,466 --> 00:08:31,974
It came natural, see with others they were trying to compete with him.

102
00:08:33,073 --> 00:08:35,891
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه is trying to compete with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

103
00:08:36,157 --> 00:08:38,315
Ali Bin Abi Talib(علي بن ابي طالب) is trying to compete with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

104
00:08:38,660 --> 00:08:43,668
But Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) is doing it as if, even if he's living alone, he's still going to do the same thing

105
00:08:44,434 --> 00:08:47,878
That was his natural way, Poet says;

106
00:08:48,605 --> 00:08:52,692
مَنْ لِي بِمِثْلِ مَشِّكَل الْمُدَلَّلِ تَمْشِي رُوَيْدًا وَتَجِي الْأَوَّلِ

107
00:08:53,592 --> 00:08:57,171
How can I compete with you, when you're walking calmly

108
00:08:57,608 --> 00:08:59,606
and with confidence and you still come the first.

109
00:09:00,324 --> 00:09:05,347
I mean, It doesn't appear that you're trying to rush it, or hasten, but you still come out the first.

110
00:09:07,304 --> 00:09:12,363
So I think that the best way to start this whole series is a statement of Ali Bin Abi Talib(علي بن ابي طالب)

111
00:09:12,387 --> 00:09:13,355
هُوَّ السَّباقْ

112
00:09:13,406 --> 00:09:14,291
he was the first.

113
00:09:15,864 --> 00:09:19,235
And I asked myself the question, how did, he do it.?

114
00:09:21,525 --> 00:09:23,200
How did he pull off such a feel.?

115
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:25,043
How did he make it.?

116
00:09:26,281 --> 00:09:29,855
You know, because as a human being, you have something against you,

117
00:09:30,841 --> 00:09:36,327
 your age, your mental abilities, body strength

118
00:09:36,850 --> 00:09:41,390
but somehow it seems that Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was able to defy all the odds.

119
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:48,122
Because in terms of body strength Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was described as being

120
00:09:48,594 --> 00:09:53,197
you know it might be a good time to give you a physical description of Abu Bakr (ابوبكر), so you could imagine him.

121
00:09:53,627 --> 00:09:54,511
See in this series,

122
00:09:54,587 --> 00:09:59,793
we want to try to not only talk about the events and affairs that happened with Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكرالصديق)

123
00:10:00,511 --> 00:10:02,889
but we want to dig deep into the personality of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

124
00:10:03,766 --> 00:10:05,303
We want to try to live with him.

125
00:10:05,739 --> 00:10:08,969
Try to see how Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) was, from the inside.

126
00:10:09,572 --> 00:10:17,140
So try to imagine, and ponder upon it, because with these people, with the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

127
00:10:17,366 --> 00:10:19,484
the more you learn about them, the more you would love them.

128
00:10:20,338 --> 00:10:24,006
See it's not like some personalities, in history they have a bright side and a dark side.

129
00:10:24,946 --> 00:10:30,169
With the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم no matter how deep you dig,

130
00:10:30,507 --> 00:10:38,251
All what you would find is good, like Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنه says About Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

131
00:10:38,495 --> 00:10:39,419
كَانَ خَيْرًا كُلَّه

132
00:10:39,844 --> 00:10:42,292
all of him was good, everything about him was good.

133
00:10:44,534 --> 00:10:48,131
So, we want to try to live with the person of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكرالصديق)

134
00:10:48,155 --> 00:10:52,373
and learn about him and see the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, every one of them was different.

135
00:10:53,496 --> 00:10:56,504
Abu Bakr (ابوبكر) was soft and compassionate, very social

136
00:10:57,040 --> 00:11:00,562
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was stern and firm.

137
00:11:01,146 --> 00:11:08,624
Now, Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) you will find this during our series of talks on As-Siddique(الصديق),

138
00:11:09,455 --> 00:11:12,650
whenever you talk about Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), you end up talking about Umar(عمر).

139
00:11:13,241 --> 00:11:16,349
And whenever you talk about Umar(عمر), you end up talking about Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

140
00:11:16,623 --> 00:11:20,221
one of them brings the other, as if they were the two wings of Islam.

141
00:11:21,693 --> 00:11:25,800
And whenever Rasool Allah ﷺ would be seen

142
00:11:26,439 --> 00:11:29,157
people would see with him Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) on one side and Umar(عمر) on the other.

143
00:11:30,098 --> 00:11:31,336
Ali Bin Abi Talib(علي بن ابي طالب) says,

144
00:11:32,959 --> 00:11:35,581
دَخَل رسول الله وَ ابو بكر وعمر

145
00:11:35,752 --> 00:11:37,700
خَرَجَ رسول الله وَ ابو بكر وعمر

146
00:11:38,363 --> 00:11:40,893
Rasool Allah ﷺ would go out with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عمر).

147
00:11:41,044 --> 00:11:42,946
And he would come back with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عمر).

148
00:11:44,167 --> 00:11:50,196
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه represents the soft and compassionate and merciful side.

149
00:11:50,486 --> 00:11:53,994
While Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) represents the punishment of Allah on evil.

150
00:11:55,042 --> 00:11:58,077
I mean, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was the worst thing that happened to Shaytaan(شيطان).

151
00:11:59,387 --> 00:12:02,175
Whenever Shaytaan(شيطان) would see Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) he would have a bad day.

152
00:12:03,250 --> 00:12:06,868
Therefore, whenever Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) would be following the path, Rasool Allah ﷺ would say

153
00:12:07,166 --> 00:12:09,364
Shaytaan(شيطان) would take another path, he would try to avoid you.

154
00:12:09,804 --> 00:12:12,252
because whenever he sees Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), he brings bad memories to him.

155
00:12:13,748 --> 00:12:16,116
So, they represent two different sides.

156
00:12:16,970 --> 00:12:20,121
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) represents Shyness.

157
00:12:20,899 --> 00:12:23,517
Ali Bin Abi Talib(علي بن ابي طالب) represents the warrior.

158
00:12:25,695 --> 00:12:30,783
With the wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ, Ayesha رضي الله عنها represents the inquisitive person, who's always asking

159
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:34,328
eager to learn knowledge, you find that a lot with, young people.

160
00:12:35,150 --> 00:12:40,505
While Khadijah رضي الله عنها, she has more of an attitude of a mature woman.

161
00:12:40,530 --> 00:12:44,370
So she was more of a psychological support of Rasool Allah ﷺ

162
00:12:44,604 --> 00:12:47,857
and whenever Rasool Allah ﷺ would need someone to lean on.

163
00:12:48,122 --> 00:12:50,915
He would find his wife Khadijah رضي الله عنها.

164
00:12:51,078 --> 00:12:53,679
So every Sahabi(صحابي), has a personality.

165
00:12:54,497 --> 00:12:56,782
And you want to learn about the personality of a Sahabi(صحابي),

166
00:12:56,866 --> 00:12:59,376
Abu Dhar(ابو زر) Al-Ghaffari رضي الله عنه, is alone.

167
00:12:59,535 --> 00:13:00,757
 In fact, there's a narration

168
00:13:01,053 --> 00:13:02,418
that he became Muslim alone,

169
00:13:02,752 --> 00:13:06,381
he dies alone, and he will be resurrected on the Day of Judgment alone.

170
00:13:07,698 --> 00:13:11,536
Because Abu Dhar Al-Ghaffari رضي الله عنه, was brought up in Ghaffar(غفار).

171
00:13:12,405 --> 00:13:15,266
Now, Ghaffar(غفار) were not businessmen like the people of Makkah

172
00:13:15,731 --> 00:13:19,419
nor were they in agriculture and farming like the people of Madina.

173
00:13:19,859 --> 00:13:23,498
The people Ghaffar(غفار), how did they make a living? By raiding caravans!

174
00:13:24,315 --> 00:13:25,394
That was their business

175
00:13:26,029 --> 00:13:28,117
raiding the caravans, of others.

176
00:13:29,018 --> 00:13:36,726
So, Abu Dhar Al-Ghaffari(ابوزرالغفاري), had to leave his people, because of their evil, he left them.

177
00:13:37,651 --> 00:13:41,539
And he lived alone in the desert, and he became Muslim alone.

178
00:13:42,098 --> 00:13:45,295
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ send him back to make Da'wah(دعوة) to his people.

179
00:13:46,013 --> 00:13:50,271
And he came back and he was successful, he brought in all of his people as Muslim.

180
00:13:51,212 --> 00:13:55,128
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ knew that ability with Abu Dhar Al-Ghaffari رضي الله عنه,

181
00:13:55,152 --> 00:13:59,940
but Rasool Allah ﷺ also knew other parts of his personality, so he told him, explicitly.

182
00:14:00,825 --> 00:14:03,861
لاَ تَأَمَّرَنَّ عَلَى اثْنَينِ، وَلاَ تَوَلَّيَنَّ مَالَ يَتِيمٍ

183
00:14:04,947 --> 00:14:08,296
Never assume responsibility even over two people,

184
00:14:09,003 --> 00:14:11,985
and never take care of the financial affairs of an orphan.

185
00:14:12,577 --> 00:14:16,022
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ knew the limitations of his personality.

186
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:19,678
He was good on one thing but some things, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him to avoid.

187
00:14:20,821 --> 00:14:24,329
Abu Darda(ابودردا), he was a Aabid(عابد), a Zahid(زاهد)

188
00:14:25,304 --> 00:14:27,333
He lives a very austere life.

189
00:14:27,886 --> 00:14:30,154
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) on the other hand was a millionaire.

190
00:14:32,007 --> 00:14:34,470
In fact, they say that Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف), when he passed away.

191
00:14:34,557 --> 00:14:36,431
Subhan Allah(سبحان الله), you know some people

192
00:14:37,187 --> 00:14:38,675
Wealth just flocks towards them.

193
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:42,152
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf رضي الله عنه, when he made Hijrah(هجرة) from Makkah to Madina

194
00:14:42,192 --> 00:14:45,435
he came broke, he had nothing, whatsoever.

195
00:14:45,808 --> 00:14:50,879
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ puts him in Akhhua(اخوة) - brotherhood with Saad Ibn Ubadah(سعد ابن عبادة),

196
00:14:51,192 --> 00:14:53,740
one of the wealthy leaders of Al-Ansaar(الانصار).

197
00:14:54,570 --> 00:14:57,120
Saad Ibn Ubadah(سعد ابن عبادة) told Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف);

198
00:14:57,660 --> 00:15:00,096
If you want I will split my wealth in two

199
00:15:00,594 --> 00:15:05,667
and I have two wives, I will divorce one of them, and marry her to you, and you choose which one you want.

200
00:15:06,363 --> 00:15:09,661
Look at the level of brotherhood, and sacrifice that Al-Ansaar(الانصار) had.

201
00:15:11,466 --> 00:15:15,214
Keep in mind that they were new Muslim, I mean it's not that they went through Tarbiah(تربيعة) for a very long time.

202
00:15:15,806 --> 00:15:18,144
They just became Muslim but they had the spirit.

203
00:15:19,363 --> 00:15:23,386
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) could have picked up this opportunity,

204
00:15:23,637 --> 00:15:27,349
half of the wealth of Saad Ibn Ubadah(سعد ابن عبادة), offered voluntarily.

205
00:15:27,620 --> 00:15:30,872
But he said: No, may Allah give you blessing in your family and your wealth.

206
00:15:31,233 --> 00:15:32,184
And then, what did he say.?

207
00:15:32,549 --> 00:15:36,399
I just want you to point out to me, where the market of Madina is.?

208
00:15:37,235 --> 00:15:38,379
دُلَّنِيْ عَلى سٌوق الْمَدينَه

209
00:15:38,403 --> 00:15:39,613
Show me where the market is.?

210
00:15:39,923 --> 00:15:40,755
That's all what I need.

211
00:15:41,105 --> 00:15:42,661
He showed him, the market of Madina

212
00:15:43,566 --> 00:15:45,224
a very short while later,

213
00:15:45,565 --> 00:15:51,430
Rasool Allah ﷺ saw Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) with some yellow powder on his face

214
00:15:51,655 --> 00:15:56,294
that yellow powder, was the makeup that they used to use, in Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة) for women.

215
00:15:57,406 --> 00:15:59,980
It was makeup for women, it's a yellow powder.

216
00:16:00,766 --> 00:16:04,042
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ asked him where is that powder from.? He said: I got married.

217
00:16:04,501 --> 00:16:06,084
So, that powder was on his face.

218
00:16:06,599 --> 00:16:08,387
He said: I got married.

219
00:16:10,203 --> 00:16:15,226
Rasool Allah ﷺ asked him and what did you pay her in Mahar(مهر), you just came from Makkah and you are broke.

220
00:16:15,488 --> 00:16:17,706
He said: I gave her gold.

221
00:16:18,868 --> 00:16:23,682
He has already made enough wealth to buy gold and give it as a Mahar(مهر) to his wife.

222
00:16:24,313 --> 00:16:28,476
When Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) passed away, or before I talked about when he passed away.

223
00:16:29,043 --> 00:16:34,281
One day, people are feeling some tremble and shaking in Madina.

224
00:16:35,214 --> 00:16:36,341
So, they asked what it was.?

225
00:16:36,381 --> 00:16:39,863
They said: The caravan of Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) has arrived from Syria.

226
00:16:41,059 --> 00:16:44,822
There are so many camels in it, you could feel the earth, shaking.

227
00:16:45,434 --> 00:16:47,275
That is how wealthy, he became.

228
00:16:47,394 --> 00:16:49,502
Allah سبحانه تعالى has blessed, his wealth.

229
00:16:49,656 --> 00:16:56,275
 Anyway, when he passed away he split up his wealth and gave it to his family members.

230
00:16:57,192 --> 00:17:03,300
But there was so much of it that he ended up separating part of his wealth and writing in his will

231
00:17:03,606 --> 00:17:07,834
that I want you to split it among all of the Muslims, who fought in the Battle of Badr(بدر)

232
00:17:09,274 --> 00:17:12,173
every one of the Muslims who fought in the battle of Badr(بدر), who were still alive

233
00:17:12,607 --> 00:17:14,663
Give him part of my inheritance.

234
00:17:15,707 --> 00:17:18,984
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) was one of the ones who fought in the Battle of Badr(بدر)

235
00:17:19,024 --> 00:17:20,567
and he was at the time a Khalifah(خليفه)

236
00:17:21,968 --> 00:17:27,616
but he still accepted his portion from the inheritance of Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف).

237
00:17:27,711 --> 00:17:29,100
Because Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) said:

238
00:17:29,386 --> 00:17:32,943
The wealth of Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) is pure Halal - 100%.

239
00:17:33,233 --> 00:17:36,962
So how can I turn down, such a gift from Allah.

240
00:17:38,056 --> 00:17:40,761
This is a wealth that has Barakah(بركة) in it, it's all Halal(حلال).

241
00:17:41,621 --> 00:17:42,774
So, how can I turn it down.

242
00:17:42,814 --> 00:17:46,122
Even though Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) himself, was he was a wealthy man

243
00:17:46,269 --> 00:17:47,197
and he was the Khalifah(خليفه).

244
00:17:48,503 --> 00:17:51,071
So, the Sahabah(صحابه) were different but it's important to learn about them.

245
00:17:51,734 --> 00:17:55,095
Why because we cannot be the same

246
00:17:56,135 --> 00:17:58,688
we have different abilities, we have different skills.

247
00:17:59,033 --> 00:18:00,879
Not everyone will be like Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب),

248
00:18:01,379 --> 00:18:04,379
nor will everyone be like the personality of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق),

249
00:18:04,915 --> 00:18:06,499
but you could be like Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاز ابن جبل),

250
00:18:06,791 --> 00:18:10,298
a scholar, or you could be a Mujahid(مجاهد) like Khalid Ibn Waleed(خالد ابن وليد).

251
00:18:10,737 --> 00:18:12,014
There are different roles.

252
00:18:12,925 --> 00:18:18,180
So, it's important to study about the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم so that you could look up to one of them

253
00:18:18,433 --> 00:18:20,137
and try to be like them.

254
00:18:20,838 --> 00:18:24,942
The one that your personality, most closely resembles

255
00:18:25,331 --> 00:18:30,872
you can take such a Sahabi(صحابي), as a role model and the same has to be said about the sisters.

256
00:18:31,614 --> 00:18:34,562
By looking at Umma Ha Tul-Moemineen(اُمَّهات المؤمنين) and looking at the Sahabiaat(صحابيات).

257
00:18:34,922 --> 00:18:37,184
Try to find for yourself a role model to follow.

258
00:18:37,925 --> 00:18:48,756
Now, our lives could be mediocre and normal - I mean, usually on a daily basis, there's not a lot happening

259
00:18:49,586 --> 00:18:51,141
not many events going on,

260
00:18:51,998 --> 00:18:56,037
but there would be a day in your life, where you where you are faced with a situation

261
00:18:56,599 --> 00:18:59,451
 that would change the course of your future.

262
00:19:00,474 --> 00:19:03,368
These are called Muaqiff(مواقف) in Arabic, it's called Muaqiff(مواقف),

263
00:19:04,784 --> 00:19:10,878
Muaqiff(مواقف) one could translate it literally, it means a standing point - It's a moment!

264
00:19:11,386 --> 00:19:15,405
It's one moment in your life, but it will change the course of your life.

265
00:19:16,274 --> 00:19:22,642
And these Muaqiff(مواقف) are the critical moments in your life that reveal, who you really are.?

266
00:19:23,154 --> 00:19:26,102
These are the tests that you will be faced with

267
00:19:26,773 --> 00:19:31,161
maybe on a daily basis, things are going normal and regular there's nothing really different.

268
00:19:31,998 --> 00:19:34,458
But there will be one day in a year or one day in a month,

269
00:19:34,498 --> 00:19:38,605
when something important will happen, and Allah is testing you through that stand.

270
00:19:39,342 --> 00:19:43,012
Where would you stand, which position will you take.?

271
00:19:44,112 --> 00:19:49,876
If we look at the life of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, we don't have his entire life record with us.

272
00:19:50,674 --> 00:19:56,049
We don't have the 365 days of every year of his life in front of us,

273
00:19:56,651 --> 00:20:01,265
but we do have a few stations in his life that tell us who Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was.

274
00:20:02,207 --> 00:20:04,627
And some of these stations were a matter of seconds.

275
00:20:05,125 --> 00:20:06,238
Some of them were longer.

276
00:20:06,976 --> 00:20:12,959
So sometimes hours or days or months could pass in your life insignificantly.

277
00:20:13,254 --> 00:20:16,352
But then one second, would make a difference.

278
00:20:17,452 --> 00:20:19,067
And that's Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

279
00:20:19,277 --> 00:20:23,449
One of you could speak one word, because of that word that would be raised up Jannah(جنة).

280
00:20:24,312 --> 00:20:27,049
And they could speak one word that would anger Allah.

281
00:20:27,129 --> 00:20:29,805
That would cause them to throw in hellfire for 70 years.

282
00:20:30,382 --> 00:20:35,400
Just one word, but that's a Muaqiff(مؤقف), that's a standing point,

283
00:20:36,118 --> 00:20:37,618
a pivotal point in your life.

284
00:20:38,467 --> 00:20:41,777
If we look at the life of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) there are many of these Muaqiff(مواقف).

285
00:20:41,864 --> 00:20:46,848
Many of these standing points, but five of them are especially unique,

286
00:20:47,483 --> 00:20:49,181
Number one, His Islam.

287
00:20:51,106 --> 00:20:56,016
With everyone else, there was a Qubwah(قبوة), you know, there's a saying in Arabic

288
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:57,713
لِكُل حسانٍ قَبْوَةْ

289
00:20:58,098 --> 00:21:00,636
For every horse, there is a stumble

290
00:21:01,473 --> 00:21:07,447
every horse, at one moment of time, it will make a slip, it will trip and fall down.

291
00:21:08,201 --> 00:21:12,095
No matter how perfect, the horse is, that will one day happen.

292
00:21:14,131 --> 00:21:19,696
Now, with every person who became Muslim, there was such a moment of hesitation

293
00:21:20,025 --> 00:21:27,203
giving it a second thought, sitting over it for a day thinking about it, with the exception of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

294
00:21:27,882 --> 00:21:30,820
As soon as the message was presented to him, he said:

295
00:21:31,237 --> 00:21:34,042
أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ مُحَمَّدًاَرَسُولَ الله

296
00:21:35,911 --> 00:21:37,216
He did not give it a second thought.

297
00:21:39,308 --> 00:21:42,322
Not because Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was an easy person to convince,

298
00:21:42,882 --> 00:21:45,740
not because Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) change his mind easily.

299
00:21:45,998 --> 00:21:49,523
In fact, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) was very decisive in his decisions.

300
00:21:49,932 --> 00:21:51,980
And that is very apparent when he became a Khalifah(خليفه).

301
00:21:52,770 --> 00:21:56,911
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه has the ability to stand up firmly,

302
00:21:57,953 --> 00:22:01,946
against all of the Sahabah(صحابه) on a few issues and in the end it turns out that he was right.

303
00:22:03,339 --> 00:22:08,087
So, it's not like a person that is, he could be easily convinced one way or another.

304
00:22:08,520 --> 00:22:10,249
- No, that wasn't the personality of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

305
00:22:10,562 --> 00:22:14,380
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) when he became Muslim, he knew exactly what he was getting his feet into.

306
00:22:15,615 --> 00:22:17,454
But we'll talk about that in his Islam.

307
00:22:17,790 --> 00:22:18,297
Why?

308
00:22:18,337 --> 00:22:21,776
why did Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) immediately accept Islam.?

309
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:26,405
Why didn't he give it a second thought - How come it was immediate? We'll get to that!

310
00:22:26,790 --> 00:22:30,313
So, this is the first Muaqiff(مؤقف) in the life of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

311
00:22:30,714 --> 00:22:38,232
The second standing point, unique point in the life of a Siddique رضي الله عنه, is Al-Israa Wal-Meraaj(الاسرآء ولمعراج)

312
00:22:39,466 --> 00:22:43,464
and I'm going through these briefly because I'll talk about them later in more detail.

313
00:22:45,262 --> 00:22:49,797
When this amazing journey happened with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

314
00:22:50,119 --> 00:22:52,998
the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) being secular people materialistic people,

315
00:22:53,038 --> 00:22:58,821
who only believe in what their eyes can see and what their ears can hear, and what their hands can touch.

316
00:23:00,242 --> 00:23:03,070
They made a joke out of Al-Israa Wal-Meraaj(الاسرآء ولمعراج), they made fun of it.

317
00:23:04,590 --> 00:23:07,851
And they thought that this is their chance to bring an end to Islam,

318
00:23:07,900 --> 00:23:13,167
all of the Muslims will give up their religion they will think that their prophet is insane.

319
00:23:14,589 --> 00:23:16,601
So, Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) was very happy.

320
00:23:17,607 --> 00:23:26,485
So they went to Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق), who wasn't there, he hasn't met with Rasool Allah ﷺ yet.

321
00:23:26,897 --> 00:23:30,594
So one of the Kuffar(كفار) went to him and said: Do you know what your friend is claiming.?

322
00:23:31,511 --> 00:23:32,705
Do you know what, he said?

323
00:23:34,463 --> 00:23:38,565
He's claiming that he has visited Jerusalem and came back in the same night.

324
00:23:40,665 --> 00:23:42,332
What was a response of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).?

325
00:23:44,197 --> 00:23:48,780
Now, if Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه had weak Eeman(ايمان).

326
00:23:49,304 --> 00:23:50,451
He would say that's not true,

327
00:23:51,126 --> 00:23:56,345
and if Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was a type of person, who could be easily deceived.

328
00:23:57,451 --> 00:23:58,762
He would say: Yes that happened.

329
00:24:00,151 --> 00:24:06,100
But Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق), since the source that is speaking to him, is one of Al-Kuffar(الكفار).

330
00:24:06,509 --> 00:24:08,185
So, can't take them at face value.

331
00:24:09,602 --> 00:24:12,215
And at the same time, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) does not want to reject

332
00:24:12,239 --> 00:24:14,508
something that Rasool Allah ﷺ could have said.

333
00:24:15,096 --> 00:24:18,770
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) said in a brief statement.

334
00:24:18,914 --> 00:24:20,562
اِنْ كَانَ قَالَهَا فَقَد صَدَقْ

335
00:24:21,986 --> 00:24:25,228
If Rasool Allah ﷺ said so, then it's the truth.

336
00:24:26,820 --> 00:24:30,963
So, there's two parts of the statement, number one, if Rasool Allah ﷺ said so.

337
00:24:30,987 --> 00:24:32,478
First of all I have to verify it.

338
00:24:32,630 --> 00:24:34,201
If he did say it, then it's the truth.

339
00:24:34,685 --> 00:24:36,667
And this is the Manhaj(منهج) of Hadith(حديث).

340
00:24:37,886 --> 00:24:39,970
That is the Manhaj(منهج) of Ulema(علماء) Al-Hadith(الحديث).

341
00:24:41,188 --> 00:24:43,164
If Rasool Allah ﷺ said it, then it's the truth.

342
00:24:43,374 --> 00:24:45,099
So, we have to verify it first.

343
00:24:45,773 --> 00:24:50,113
We don't just accept it, at face value, when the narration could be weak

344
00:24:50,405 --> 00:24:51,699
we have to study the narration.

345
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:55,103
 If it's established, that it's Sahih(صحيح), we won't reject it.

346
00:24:55,542 --> 00:25:03,150
We won't turn it down, we won't say it is illogical, this goes against the civilized, 21st century, No!.

347
00:25:03,321 --> 00:25:04,977
We would accept it.

348
00:25:05,726 --> 00:25:09,951
As long as Rasool Allah ﷺ said it, then it's right, it's true, it's Wahii(وحي) from Allah.

349
00:25:11,795 --> 00:25:16,636
The third standing point is during the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

350
00:25:16,946 --> 00:25:20,018
The historians, describe that moment, by saying:

351
00:25:20,531 --> 00:25:26,105
when Rasool Allah ﷺ died, Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) was hiding in his house.

352
00:25:28,466 --> 00:25:34,065
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was carrying his sword and claiming that Muhammadﷺ did not die,

353
00:25:34,679 --> 00:25:38,737
but he went to meet Allah for 40 days, like Musa(موسى) went to meet Allah and he will be back.

354
00:25:39,114 --> 00:25:42,182
And whoever claims that Muhammad(محمد) has died, I will cut off his head.

355
00:25:43,559 --> 00:25:46,398
And some of the Sahabah(صحابه) were in the Masjid(مسجد), crying.

356
00:25:47,394 --> 00:25:52,292
That's how they give a description of the situation in Madina after Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away.

357
00:25:53,447 --> 00:25:57,745
