536
00:40:25,872 --> 00:40:28,166
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) subdue them in the end

537
00:40:28,206 --> 00:40:32,179
and they came to realize, who Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) really was!

538
00:40:32,729 --> 00:40:34,552
Anyway, so that was name Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

539
00:40:35,357 --> 00:40:38,305
The titles that were given to him, the most famous one is As-Siddique(الصديق),

540
00:40:38,619 --> 00:40:41,186
which is derived from As-Siddq(الصدق) truth.

541
00:40:41,556 --> 00:40:43,175
Why was he given that name?

542
00:40:43,317 --> 00:40:47,519
Well, there are a few instances that happened in his life.

543
00:40:48,227 --> 00:40:52,685
The one that Ayesha(عائشه) mentions, she says, she mentions the story of Al-Israa(الاسرآء).

544
00:40:52,878 --> 00:40:54,703
If he said it, then is the truth.

545
00:40:54,949 --> 00:40:59,139
So Ayesha(عائشه) say, he was called As-Siddique(الصديق), the believing

546
00:40:59,619 --> 00:41:01,623
- and this is narrated in Al-Hakim(الحاكم).

547
00:41:02,485 --> 00:41:05,883
Rasool Allah ﷺ has also called him As-Siddique(الصديق).

548
00:41:07,125 --> 00:41:12,189
Rasool Allah ﷺ one day was standing on Uhud(أحَد) along with Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) and Umar(عمر) and Uthman(عثمان).

549
00:41:13,049 --> 00:41:17,700
So there was a slight earthquake. So, Rasool Allah ﷺ put his hand on the mountain and said,

550
00:41:17,724 --> 00:41:18,474
أثْبُتْ أحُدْ

551
00:41:18,498 --> 00:41:25,136
Uhud(أحَد) stay firm. Because on top of you, is a prophet, a Siddique(الصديق) and two martyrs

552
00:41:27,791 --> 00:41:29,669
- and the mountain stopped moving.

553
00:41:30,038 --> 00:41:34,229
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ called Abu Bakr - As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق), and he called Umar(عمر) and Uthman(عثمان) - Shuhadah(شهداء).

554
00:41:34,920 --> 00:41:37,838
اِنَّما عَلَيك نَبِيٌ وَصديق وَشَهِيْدَيْنْ

555
00:41:39,303 --> 00:41:43,285
He was also called As-Siddique(الصديق) because he was very fast in accepting Islam.

556
00:41:43,765 --> 00:41:48,973
And this is the most famous name, another name given to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is As-Sahibb(الصاحب)

557
00:41:49,620 --> 00:41:50,251
- The companion.

558
00:41:51,390 --> 00:41:56,308
All of the Sahabah(صحابه) were companions, but the companionship of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was unique

559
00:41:58,042 --> 00:42:01,172
Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) had special relationship.

560
00:42:02,073 --> 00:42:07,497
They were very close together, even before Islam. And they were close in age.

561
00:42:08,430 --> 00:42:11,608
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) was only two years younger than Rasool Allah ﷺ.

562
00:42:11,632 --> 00:42:16,573
- While the other Sahabah(صحابه) were very young. And Ali Bin Abi Talib(علي بن ابي طالب) was a child.

563
00:42:16,974 --> 00:42:19,993
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was considered to be among the seniors of As-Sahabah(الصحابه),

564
00:42:20,180 --> 00:42:22,086
he was only 28 years old when he became Muslim.

565
00:42:23,402 --> 00:42:28,953
However, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was 38, when he became Muslim, so he was among the closest of the Sahabah(صحابه)

566
00:42:29,259 --> 00:42:31,392
- to the age of Muhammadﷺ.

567
00:42:32,460 --> 00:42:35,984
Rasool Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) had a very close relationship before Islam

568
00:42:36,837 --> 00:42:40,751
- very close friendship and Islam only strengthen it further.

569
00:42:42,660 --> 00:42:47,722
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was so close to Muhammadﷺ as if he was created for him

570
00:42:48,988 --> 00:42:52,858
- I mean Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was not only a friend, he was a companion

571
00:42:53,346 --> 00:42:54,201
 an advisor

572
00:42:55,211 --> 00:42:56,490
a financial supporter

573
00:42:56,965 --> 00:42:57,785
a bodyguard

574
00:42:58,156 --> 00:42:58,884
a confident

575
00:42:59,687 --> 00:43:01,996
 he was everything for Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

576
00:43:02,872 --> 00:43:05,650
And this name was given to Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) in Qur'an.

577
00:43:07,281 --> 00:43:11,484
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says about the journey of Al-Hijrah(الحجرة).

578
00:43:12,456 --> 00:43:14,970
إِلَّا تَنْصُرُوهُ فَقَدْ نَصَرَهُ اللَّهُ

579
00:43:15,448 --> 00:43:20,206
 إِذْ أَخْرَجَهُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا ثَانِيَ اثْنَيْنِ إِذْ هُمَا فِي الْغَارِ إِذْ يَقُولُ لِصَاحِبِهِ

580
00:43:20,668 --> 00:43:22,622
لَا تَحْزَنْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَنَا

581
00:43:23,529 --> 00:43:27,635
فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ سَكِينَتَهُ عَلَيْهِ وَأَيَّدَهُ بِجُنُودٍ لَمْ تَرَوْهَا

582
00:43:28,774 --> 00:43:33,889
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says, If you do not aid him, Allah has already aided him.

583
00:43:34,504 --> 00:43:42,701
When those, who disbelieved had driven him out, as one of two, when they were in the cave and he said to his companion.

584
00:43:43,325 --> 00:43:50,469
So, he is called in Qur'an, the companion of Muhammadﷺ, do not grieve, Indeed Allah is with us.

585
00:43:51,331 --> 00:43:56,929
And Allah sent down his tranquility upon him, and supported him with soldiers, you did not see

586
00:43:57,377 --> 00:44:02,895
- and made the word of those who disbelieved, the lowest, while the word of Allah that is the highest

587
00:44:03,256 --> 00:44:05,490
- and Allah is Exalted in Might and Wise.

588
00:44:06,867 --> 00:44:09,581
Ibn Hajar Al-Asqalani(ابن حجر العسقلاني) comments on this Ayah(آية), and says,

589
00:44:10,561 --> 00:44:14,409
فإن المراد بصاحبه هنا أبو بكر بلا منازع،

590
00:44:15,648 --> 00:44:22,404
والأحاديث في كونه كان معه في الغار كثيرة مشهورة، ولم يشركه في المنقبة غيره

591
00:44:23,435 --> 00:44:28,094
Ibn Hajar(ابن حجر) says, the companion in this Ayah(آية) is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

592
00:44:28,598 --> 00:44:33,896
according to the consensus of the scholars and there are many ahadith(احاديث) to state that.

593
00:44:34,328 --> 00:44:40,606
And there is no one, who shared this unique quality with Rasool Allah ﷺ except Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

594
00:44:41,428 --> 00:44:46,706
Another name is Al-Ateeq(العتيق), Al-Ateeq(العتيق) means the emancipated.

595
00:44:47,622 --> 00:44:51,510
- The one who's freed from slavery, the one who is liberated.

596
00:44:52,642 --> 00:44:56,425
Now Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) is never really a slave in the worldly sense

597
00:44:56,449 --> 00:44:57,721
- so what is meant by Al-Ateeq(العتيق)?

598
00:44:59,201 --> 00:45:05,413
Because when the slave is freed, Al-Atq(العتق), freeing slaves is Al-Atq(العتق),

599
00:45:05,925 --> 00:45:09,733
so Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) was called Al-Ateeq(العتيق), the one who's freed, emancipated.

600
00:45:10,634 --> 00:45:17,195
What is meant by this Ayesha رضي الله عنها says, That Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه came to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

601
00:45:18,191 --> 00:45:20,012
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ looked at him and said:

602
00:45:20,036 --> 00:45:23,312
أبشر يا ابا بكر فأنت عتيق اللـه من النار

603
00:45:24,094 --> 00:45:30,589
O Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), receive the glad tidings and rejoice. You are the freed slave of Allah, from hellfire.

604
00:45:31,720 --> 00:45:36,644
He's also called Al-Atqaa(العتقه). Al-Atqaa(العتقه) means the most pious.

605
00:45:38,616 --> 00:45:41,666
And he was given that title in Qur'an In Surat Al-Lail(سورة اليل),

606
00:45:41,884 --> 00:45:45,457
وَسَيُجَنَّبُهَا الْأَتْقَى ۝ الَّذِي يُؤْتِي مَالَهُ يَتَزَكَّىٰ۝

607
00:45:46,060 --> 00:45:51,935
The reasoning behind this, is that Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) and we'll talk about the details of this.

608
00:45:53,709 --> 00:45:57,392
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) used to free slaves, the Muslim slaves,

609
00:45:58,431 --> 00:46:02,590
who were under persecution he would buy them and free them.

610
00:46:04,329 --> 00:46:07,302
But the slaves he would free, were weak, women.

611
00:46:08,142 --> 00:46:12,041
Now, the tradition was in Arabia that when you free a slave,

612
00:46:12,682 --> 00:46:20,434
that slave retains a relationship of loyalty with you because you are the one who freed the slave.

613
00:46:20,734 --> 00:46:25,113
So, slave has special loyalty with you when they're freed.

614
00:46:25,837 --> 00:46:30,404
 It's not a relationship of slavery anymore but it's a relationship of strong loyalty.

615
00:46:31,781 --> 00:46:34,519
The father of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), went to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and told him my son,

616
00:46:34,840 --> 00:46:38,778
how come you are freeing these weak slaves, women and children?

617
00:46:39,243 --> 00:46:43,862
Why don't you free, if you're going to free slaves, why don't you free some strong men?

618
00:46:44,168 --> 00:46:45,880
- so that one day they will support you.?

619
00:46:46,581 --> 00:46:48,213
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said:

620
00:46:48,237 --> 00:46:49,876
The reason I'm doing this is to please Allah

621
00:46:51,126 --> 00:46:56,843
I'm not looking for any worldly benefit. So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed the last Ayaat(آيات) in Surat Ul Lail(سورة اليل),

622
00:46:57,482 --> 00:46:58,859
وَسَيُجَنَّبُهَا الْأَتْقَى ۝

623
00:46:59,204 --> 00:47:00,934
الَّذِي يُؤْتِي مَالَهُ يَتَزَكَّىٰ ۝

624
00:47:01,220 --> 00:47:03,515
وَمَا لِأَحَدٍ عِنْدَهُ مِنْ نِعْمَةٍ تُجْزَىٰ ۝ إ

625
00:47:03,799 --> 00:47:06,362
ِلَّا ابْتِغَاءَ وَجْهِ رَبِّهِ الْأَعْلَىٰ ۝ وَلَسَوْفَ يَرْضَىٰ۝

626
00:47:07,267 --> 00:47:11,498
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says But the righteous one, will avoid it.

627
00:47:12,092 --> 00:47:19,207
He, who gives from his wealth to purify himself and not giving for anyone who has done him a favor to be rewarded.

628
00:47:19,266 --> 00:47:22,895
He's not paying back anyone he is not doing it for a reward himself,

629
00:47:23,257 --> 00:47:28,616
but only seeking the countenance of his Lord most high and he is going to be satisfied.

630
00:47:29,531 --> 00:47:32,241
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says, he is going to be satisfied.

631
00:47:32,892 --> 00:47:34,881
Allahعَزّوجَلّ will make Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) happy.

632
00:47:36,486 --> 00:47:43,034
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was born two years after the year of the elephant,

633
00:47:43,745 --> 00:47:45,941
because the Arabs did not have a calendar system.

634
00:47:46,428 --> 00:47:51,221
So, whenever an important event would happen, they would call that year after this event.

635
00:47:51,301 --> 00:47:56,277
So when Allah destroyed the army of Abraha(ابراهة) that year was called Aam El- Feel(عام الفيل), the year of the elephant.

636
00:47:57,075 --> 00:48:00,413
Later on, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) developed the calendar

637
00:48:00,639 --> 00:48:07,237
- because Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) when he became Khalifah(خليفه), there were a few cases that were taken to court.

638
00:48:07,582 --> 00:48:13,948
For example, you would say I gave that person a loan. And here's the contract, you pay me back in Shaban(شعبان).

639
00:48:14,325 --> 00:48:17,663
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: The problem is, it doesn't say Shaban(شعبان) which year

640
00:48:18,357 --> 00:48:19,381
they didn't have a calendar.

641
00:48:20,158 --> 00:48:24,412
So, it just say, Shaban(شعبان), Shaban(شعبان) this year, last year, 10 years from now.

642
00:48:24,747 --> 00:48:26,642
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: We have to sort that thing out

643
00:48:26,963 --> 00:48:28,557
- we have to have our calendar.

644
00:48:28,858 --> 00:48:30,144
 Now, Islam is a Khilafah(خلافه).

645
00:48:30,471 --> 00:48:35,860
It's not within a small group where everybody knows each other, we have to establish a system.

646
00:48:36,554 --> 00:48:40,808
And that's when they adopted Al-Hijrah(الهجره) but before that it was the year of the elephant.

647
00:48:41,708 --> 00:48:45,739
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) was born two years after the year of the elephant

648
00:48:45,763 --> 00:48:51,179
- and Rasool Allah ﷺ was born a few weeks after the event of the elephant.

649
00:48:51,938 --> 00:48:54,200
So, there was a two year difference between them.

650
00:48:55,371 --> 00:48:58,395
I want to give you a physical description of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

651
00:48:59,375 --> 00:49:04,121
- it's not much that exists, but at least you can develop a mental picture of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

652
00:49:04,236 --> 00:49:11,231
because you imagine a certain image of a person and that image could be wrong.

653
00:49:11,743 --> 00:49:16,766
Now the image helps you understand about the person when you look at the person.

654
00:49:16,879 --> 00:49:18,292
Especially if you have Farasah(فراسه),

655
00:49:19,077 --> 00:49:23,513
Farasah(فراسه) is the art of reading the face, you could tell a lot about that person

656
00:49:23,537 --> 00:49:29,144
- and the Arabs used to study this science and it says that Ash-Shafie(الشافعي) went to study Farasah(فراسه) in Yemen.

657
00:49:29,168 --> 00:49:33,974
So it was a science that was taught or an art actually, it is reading the face.

658
00:49:34,391 --> 00:49:37,205
It says that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was one of the people, who were good at it.

659
00:49:37,836 --> 00:49:44,069
He saw someone and he asked him, what's your name? He said: My name is flame.

660
00:49:44,414 --> 00:49:47,163
He said, What's your family name?

661
00:49:47,604 --> 00:49:49,366
He said: My family name is Spark.

662
00:49:49,781 --> 00:49:53,189
What's his tribe name? He said: My tribe name is fire.

663
00:49:53,582 --> 00:49:57,111
He said: Well go back home because your house is on fire and it turned out to be true.

664
00:49:58,186 --> 00:50:00,075
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) saw another man.

665
00:50:00,297 --> 00:50:06,218
He just looked at his face and said: This man is a magician, or he was a magician,

666
00:50:07,549 --> 00:50:11,453
So, they call the man and he said: Yes, I used to be a sorcerer in Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة).

667
00:50:12,394 --> 00:50:13,524
He saw it, in his face.

668
00:50:13,751 --> 00:50:18,548
So then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) asked him, What is the strangest thing that you heard from Al-Jinn(الجن)?

669
00:50:18,866 --> 00:50:24,039
So, he mentioned some poetry that was talking about the coming of Muhammadﷺ, that he heard from Al-Jinn(الجن)

670
00:50:24,622 --> 00:50:31,044
so you want to develop a mental picture and again, you'll find the contrasting,

671
00:50:31,393 --> 00:50:32,937
mental picture between Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عمر).

672
00:50:34,194 --> 00:50:41,620
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was medium to short in height and he was very slim, slender.

673
00:50:42,616 --> 00:50:43,855
In fact extremely slim.

674
00:50:45,751 --> 00:50:49,021
When Rasool Allah ﷺ said that you have should have your Izaar(إزار) above the ankle.

675
00:50:49,337 --> 00:50:55,161
Al-Izaar(الإزار) is like a towel or a Longi(لونكي), but a Longi(لونكى) is a the tide is circular

676
00:50:55,615 --> 00:51:01,176
the Izaar(ازار) is open, they would wrap one towel on the bottom half.

677
00:51:01,728 --> 00:51:05,758
And if they have enough money, then they would buy a second piece to cover their top

678
00:51:06,413 --> 00:51:08,707
- Otherwise they would not cover the shoulders.

679
00:51:09,338 --> 00:51:13,476
That was it, like Al-Ihraam(الاحرام) basically that was their clothes.

680
00:51:13,500 --> 00:51:19,031
Obviously there were different types of clothes that they had, but this was the predominant one.

681
00:51:19,551 --> 00:51:22,630
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) when he heard Rasool Allah ﷺ say

682
00:51:22,654 --> 00:51:26,429
that the Izaar(ازار) should be above the ankle. He went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said:

683
00:51:26,453 --> 00:51:29,156
يا رسول الله اِنَّ اَزاري لَا يَسْتَمْسِكُو على حقوي

684
00:51:29,930 --> 00:51:33,569
O messenger of Allah, my Izaar(ازار) is not holding on to my waist.

685
00:51:34,566 --> 00:51:39,134
He was so slim that his Izaar(ازار) would not hold to his waist and it would fall down.

686
00:51:39,534 --> 00:51:45,051
So the Izaar(ازار) would go under the ankle. So, is there anything wrong with that?

687
00:51:45,075 --> 00:51:46,594
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No! not for you.

688
00:51:47,653 --> 00:51:52,507
That is how slim Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) was, the Izaar(ازار) wouldn't even hold on his waist

689
00:51:52,531 --> 00:52:01,160
- and he was described as having very slim legs. In fact, his entire body, didn't have a lot of flesh, even his face

690
00:52:01,854 --> 00:52:03,430
- you could see the bones on his cheek,

691
00:52:04,347 --> 00:52:05,641
وكان غارالعينين

692
00:52:05,666 --> 00:52:11,163
And his eyes were deep in the socket. And he was very fair skin.

693
00:52:12,062 --> 00:52:14,391
He was described as being white, Abyadh(ابيض).

694
00:52:14,538 --> 00:52:22,493
Now, this is obviously relative because the Arabs when they would say white, it meant fair skin.

695
00:52:24,719 --> 00:52:32,181
But what we call white now they would call red, when they would say that a person is red or yellow, it means white.

696
00:52:32,676 --> 00:52:38,585
So, don't take the words literally the colors literally when you're reading old Arabic text,

697
00:52:39,184 --> 00:52:49,830
because they would call for example the Europeans Bannu Ul Asfar(بنو الاصفر) the yellow people and Ahmar(احمر) is

698
00:52:49,854 --> 00:52:56,742
they would also call them sometimes Ahmar(احمر), red. White was fair skin relative to the people in the desert

699
00:52:57,032 --> 00:53:04,385
- because usually the people in desert have dark skin. So, relative to that Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) was fair skin.

700
00:53:05,945 --> 00:53:11,026
He was very social person. He was very approachable and likeable.

701
00:53:11,942 --> 00:53:17,415
Now with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), on the other hand, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was very tall, well built.

702
00:53:17,983 --> 00:53:20,182
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was anything but slim.

703
00:53:21,181 --> 00:53:23,313
